# Signal Relay — Telegram → MT5

Reads trading signals from selected Telegram chats on **your account**,
parses them, executes on **MetaTrader 5** (whatever account is logged into
the running terminal — currently MetaQuotes-Demo), and reports everything
into your Hermes chat.

## Files
| file | role |
|---|---|
| `parser.py` | free-text signal → structured trade (symbol/side/entry/SL/TPs) |
| `executor.py` | MT5 order placement with risk guard + ledger (`signals.db`) |
| `manage.py` | break-even + trailing-stop engine (run alongside daemon) |
| `notify.py` | pushes reports into the Hermes Telegram chat |
| `daemon.py` | Telegram listener (Telethon, your account) — drives everything |
| `config.json` | all knobs: channels, mode, risk limits, sizing, BE/trail |

## First-time setup (needs api_id/api_hash once)
1. Get credentials at https://my.telegram.org → API development tools.
2. `python daemon.py --login` — stores the session (one-time).
3. `python daemon.py --list-dialogs` — prints your chats + IDs.
4. Put the signal-channel IDs into `config.json` → `"channels": [...]`.
5. Start: `python daemon.py` (listener) and `python manage.py` (BE/trail).

## Operating
- **HALT** file next to daemon.py → blocks NEW trades instantly; relay keeps reporting. Delete to resume.
- **STOP** file → stops daemon + manager.
- All trades logged in `signals.db` (sqlite) — ask Hermes for a status/P-L report anytime.
- Modes: `"mode": "auto"` executes immediately (risk-guarded); `"confirm"` posts parsed signal and waits for your approval in chat.

## Risk guard (executor.py)
- max lot per trade, max open positions, max trades/day, symbol allowlist,
  duplicate-signal block (per message id), SL/TP validation (distance, side sanity),
  free-margin floor. Sizing: risk-% of balance from SL distance (default 1%) or fixed lots.

## Safety facts
- Executes on the account logged into the running MT5 terminal — currently MetaQuotes-Demo login 5057394166 (USD, $100k demo; the account was switched Oct 14 — earlier it was 113783047).
- MT5 auto-starts at Windows logon via `Startup/mt5-autostart.bat`.
- Telegram leg only READS the chats you list; it never posts there.
